    <div class="chart-box">
      <h4>Distribution by Age</h4>
      <canvas id="chartAge" height="240"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h4>Parent Education Level</h4>
      <canvas id="chartParentEd" height="240"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <h4>Internet Access &amp; Private Tuition</h4>
      <canvas id="chartAccess" height="240"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Key Demographic Observations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Gender balance:</strong> Near-equal split (51% female, 49% male).</li>
    <li><strong>District representation:</strong> Chattogram leads with 133 students; all eight divisions have 117&ndash;133 students, ensuring comparability.</li>
    <li><strong>Age distribution:</strong> Ages 15&ndash;17 each contribute ~26%, with 18-year-olds at 21.1%.</li>
    <li><strong>School type:</strong> A slight majority (52.4%) attend private schools.</li>
    <li><strong>Parent education:</strong> Fairly even across all four levels (23.5%&ndash;26.7%), with Graduates the largest group (26.7%).</li>
    <li><strong>Internet access:</strong> 47.8% have home internet; 52.2% do not.</li>
    <li><strong>Private tuition:</strong> Almost exactly split &mdash; 50.3% receive private tuition.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS -->
<div class="section" id="sec2">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number">2</div>
    <h2>Academic Performance Analysis</h2>
  </div>
  <p>This section examines the distribution and progression of academic outcomes across three GPA metrics: Previous GPA, SSC Result, and HSC Result.</p>

  <div class="stat-grid">
    <div class="stat-box"><div class="val">3.995</div><div class="lbl">Mean Previous GPA</div></div>
